e/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/3e475d534a8f090caa9611d865e70a9717969ddc541c55d98200e19031bffe84.png" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534466 true] [17592186289820 1111 #uuid "53b0e08e-406e-5506-8b7d-bc2a778b94db" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289821 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/95b3d8fc43562341f93a2bccbcbe36d2a070a2dd6687606175ab5e9580f86e2f.png" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289821 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534466 true] [17592186289821 1111 #uuid "5d99d12f-c09f-538f-a9f4-426942ead7ed" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289822 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/0d14e369d621a6c2d06b4db1485ff43f6af4be2014e9d26564c9ca11e9bd38cd.png" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289822 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534466 true] [17592186289822 1111 #uuid "e69ac199-3b5b-5b77-9585-00467bfaa84a" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289823 1017 #edb/ref 17592186289824 13194139534466 true] [17592186289823 1089 "q-352068" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289823 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534466 true] [17592186289823 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{x+1}\\,{y}^{′}=4$ that satisfies the condition $y(3)=10.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289823 1113 #uuid "c774207f-e833-51f4-b6a4-47a8e4f76e5c" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289823 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =4\\int (x+1)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(2(x+1)^{1/2})+C \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{x+1}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=8\\sqrt{x+1}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(3)=10$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =8\\sqrt{3+1}+C \\\\ 10 & =8(2)+C \\\\ C & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=8\\sqrt{x+1}-6.\n$$" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289824 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289825 13194139534466 true] [17592186289824 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534466 true] [17592186289824 1041 "field-1" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289824 1104 #edb/ref 17592186289825 13194139534466 true] [17592186289824 1110 #uuid "27fbb802-818f-528e-a38b-34520e907660" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289825 1034 "8\\sqrt{x+1}-6" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289825 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534466 true] [17592186289825 1111 #uuid "4a772853-58d2-56db-991e-ec65fe8d0aa9" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289826 1017 #edb/ref 17592186289827 13194139534466 true] [17592186289826 1089 "q-49947" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289826 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534466 true] [17592186289826 1100 "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ for $x>0?$" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289826 1113 #uuid "0290b966-ea8a-5aaa-95c5-d4ed0c24c604" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289826 1145 "Rearranging and Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C,\\,x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/8e047c3c27a000af943f50499f8c7559acceeb78cc006e796c7d353729991517.png)" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289828 13194139534466 true] [17592186289827 1000 #edb/ref 17