/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/aae99f368b61351b9163646b70ea0b085019d6935334422ccb398958a81d1e47.png" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289832 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534466 true] [17592186289832 1111 #uuid "36962595-cfc5-5593-8096-3776d0d8346d" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289833 1017 #edb/ref 17592186289834 13194139534466 true] [17592186289833 1089 "q-50146" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289833 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534466 true] [17592186289833 1100 "Solve the differential equation $x\\cdot \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}.$" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289833 1113 #uuid "a6ab78bb-c8ea-5de6-abd1-a27ba2080dba" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289833 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-4x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-4(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-2(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289835 13194139534466 true] [17592186289834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289836 13194139534466 true] [17592186289834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289837 13194139534466 true] [17592186289834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289838 13194139534466 true] [17592186289834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289839 13194139534466 true] [17592186289834 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534466 true] [17592186289834 1041 "selection" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289834 1104 #edb/ref 17592186289837 13194139534466 true] [17592186289834 1110 #uuid "53fdc3f8-2079-5b4a-b8fc-969e00cb264d" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289835 1034 "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289835 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534466 true] [17592186289835 1111 #uuid "113c25f7-34d8-597a-9d18-6e2a6ffa7ace" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289836 1034 "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534466 true] [17592186289836 1111 #uuid "32d3c70f-8bd8-5ce8-b6f6-f8e361f906a5" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289837 1034 "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289837 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534466 true] [17592186289837 1111 #uuid "a0491e6f-f72a-552c-a54d-7b7411e89373" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289838 1034 "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+Cx+D" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534466 true] [17592186289838 1111 #uuid "3b8ba3ba-6fed-5713-a29b-e5a693af1a4e" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289839 1034 "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C{x}^{2}+D" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534466 true] [17592186289839 1111 #uuid "73a3e9fd-1914-52e9-a145-05bd26f2d97d" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289840 1017 #edb/ref 17592186289841 13194139534466 true] [17592186289840 1089 "q-50197" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289840 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534466 true] [17592186289840 1100 "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1=0$ for $x>0?$" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289840 1113 #uuid "a4a52539-fba9-529d-8223-251824b4bbce" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289840 1145 "Rearranging and Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1$ for $x>0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/c837c3b617fa49f3d081d961196a954fada99b8d7cd12b7d7f729232e16be066.png)" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289842 13194139534466 true] [17592186289841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289843 13194139534466 true] [17592186289841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289844 13194139534466 true] [17592186289841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289845 13194139534466 true] [17592186289841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289846 13194139534466 true] [17592186289841 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534466 true] [17592186289841 1041 "selection" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289841 1104 #edb/ref 17592186289843 13194139534466 true] [17592186289841 1110 #uuid "97a3a653-59a6-54f3-b434-8384602bd8e4" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289842 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/18a0a935932bbe409ceb7e36459a2091ee46b74829c873bfc048a71f543d8eff.png" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534466 true] [17592186289842 1111 #uuid "cd855587-99f3-505e-97c3-1301d8ab4a63" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289843 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/90beec07c4d15fa823aee98c8a1a1e6c58846bb9b713b84848e010cc98cb3ca3.png" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534466 true] [17592186289843 1111 #uuid "7b7db587-abe5-59ed-bd47-170916b1d8a2" 13194139534466 true] [17592186289844 1034 "/home/jake/Dev